From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Vogelaar <revogelaar@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 10:20:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] snmp: find existing subagents across users

run_subagent.sh runs as root, but each snmp_subagent changes to the non-root
account.  `ps -ww` retains the default effective-UID selection, so the wrapper
does not find or stop an existing subagent before launching another one.

Use pidof to preserve the wrapper's existing replace-all behavior across UID
boundaries.  Guard the kill so an empty process set is a normal first-start
case rather than an invalid kill invocation.

This complements the self-heal caller fix: the caller no longer schedules a
replacement for a live process, while the wrapper remains idempotent if it is
invoked explicitly or races another recovery path.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Rob Vogelaar <revogelaar@gmail.com>
---
 scripts/run_subagent.sh | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/scripts/run_subagent.sh b/scripts/run_subagent.sh
index 5fc6477..8068629 100755
--- a/scripts/run_subagent.sh
+++ b/scripts/run_subagent.sh
@@ -68,8 +68,10 @@ if [ ! -f /tmp/ccsp_msg.cfg ]; then
 
 master=$1 # may empty
 
-SNMP_PID=`ps -ww | grep snmp_subagent | grep -v cm_snmp_ma_2 | grep -v grep | awk '{print $1}'`
-kill -9 $SNMP_PID
+SNMP_PID=$(pidof snmp_subagent)
+if [ -n "$SNMP_PID" ]; then
+    kill -9 $SNMP_PID
+fi
 
 if [ "x$master" != "x" ]; then
       if [[ "$BOX_TYPE" = "XB3" && "$ENABLE_SNMPv2" = "true" || "$BOX_TYPE" != "XB3" ]]; then
-- 
